    "proximity": "A centerline is near the other source where its clipped geometry falls inside a 20 m buffer of that source. Twenty metres covers a lane-scale offset between two digitizations. It is not a segment match.",
    "name_agreement": "Names are uppercased, apostrophes and hyphens are removed, and a trailing abbreviation such as RD or ST is expanded. An OSM tag with several names separated by semicolons contributes each name. A name with no street suffix agrees with the same words plus one suffix, so Broadmead agrees with Broadmead Street. Different suffixes do not agree, and a spacing difference does not agree. A length agrees when it lies within 20 m of at least one equivalent name. A centerline may be near several names. No centerline is assigned a partner id.",
    "one_source": "Length beyond the 20 m buffer is in one source only for this proximity. A centerline is listed as mostly one source when at least half of its clipped length, and at least 50 m, is beyond the buffer. Names present in one inventory only are a separate list: the same road can carry two names.",
    "drive_like": "Primary, secondary, local, and ramp (S1100, S1200, S1400, S1630) are reported beside the full NJOGIS total. The full total is the length compared with OSM."
  },
